The talktome source code uses the MIT license. See LICENSE.
Its dependencies keep their own licenses.

Packaged app

The packaged macOS app is built with Electron (MIT), which includes Chromium
and its third-party components. The app bundle includes their license files.

talktome-server

talktome-server installs from PyPI with its dependencies, which include the
Model Context Protocol Python SDK (MIT). Each keeps its own license.

Local speech detection

Silero voice activity detection (VAD) uses the MIT license. Smart Turn uses the BSD 2-Clause license.
The app includes their license texts in its voice resources.
The detection process uses NumPy, ONNX Runtime, and Transformers. Each keeps its own license.

Services

Speech uses ElevenLabs with the user's own API key. The user's ElevenLabs
account terms apply to that use.
